"Every setting Sova has: this project's, its merge queue's and the Sova-wide ones. You only prepare a card; the person applies it with a click on Sova's own page, and you can neither apply nor undo one. Even a change that narrows waits for them. get: every setting with its state, the cards waiting. reference {setting}: one setting's keys and what needs the person's approval. propose {why, edits}: prepare a card. A project edit is as the reference says; a merge queue edit is {setting: \"merge-queue\", changes?, models?}, on a card of its own; which existing Claude login a project uses is {setting: \"claude-login\", login}; a Sova-wide edit is {setting: \"sova\", id, value}, on a card of its own. withdraw {card}: drop a card you prepared (sc_… or sw_…). Keys, tokens and sign-ins never go on a card: a card that carries one is refused, and the person signs in the supported way."
